WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.180
The travelers walked up the Spirit Mountain.

2
00:00:06.181 --> 00:00:13.473
The mountain's slopes were covered in pine trees, bamboo, and flowers.

3
00:00:13.474 --> 00:00:17.770
Birds sang, and small animals ran by.

4
00:00:17.771 --> 00:00:22.504
The Tang Monk stopped walking and turned to his companions.

5
00:00:22.505 --> 00:00:25.850
"I want to thank you all," said the monk.

6
00:00:25.851 --> 00:00:29.568
"You have helped me to reach the Western Paradise.

7
00:00:29.569 --> 00:00:32.803
You saved me from demons countless times.

8
00:00:32.804 --> 00:00:35.684
I couldn't have gotten here without you."

9
00:00:35.685 --> 00:00:38.183
[g@Wukong laughed.

10
00:00:38.184 --> 00:00:40.617
"You don't need to thank us, Master.@g]

11
00:00:40.618 --> 00:00:42.354
[g@We all helped each other.

12
00:00:42.355 --> 00:00:45.286
You helped me to be good.@g]

13
00:00:45.287 --> 00:00:50.255
Now I will earn forgiveness for the evil things I did long ago."

14
00:00:50.256 --> 00:00:51.656
[g@Wujing nodded.

15
00:00:51.657 --> 00:00:56.054
"And I will earn forgiveness for breaking that glass in Heaven."@g]

16
00:00:56.055 --> 00:01:01.390
"I will earn forgiveness for causing trouble in Heaven too," added Bajie.

17
00:01:01.391 --> 00:01:04.257
He waved a hand toward the horse.

18
00:01:04.258 --> 00:01:08.080
"And remember—that horse is really a dragon.

19
00:01:08.081 --> 00:01:11.836
He accidentally set fire to his father's palace.

20
00:01:11.837 --> 00:01:15.536
He too will earn forgiveness."

21
00:01:15.537 --> 00:01:17.129
[g@Wukong smiled.

22
00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:23.220
"See, Master? We are all thankful."@g]

23
00:01:23.221 --> 00:01:30.576
They continued up the mountain and were soon surrounded by clouds.

24
00:01:30.577 --> 00:01:35.311
Bright light shone from the Thunderclap Monastery above.

25
00:01:35.312 --> 00:01:40.134
The travelers arrived at an enormous gate, where two guards stood.

26
00:01:40.135 --> 00:01:47.924
Beyond the gate the Thunderclap Monastery's towers and arches sparkled with bright light.

27
00:01:47.925 --> 00:01:50.713
"Greetings," said the monk to the guards.

28
00:01:50.714 --> 00:01:56.379
"I am the Tang Monk, and I'm here to receive the True Scriptures from Buddha."

29
00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:01.837
"You may enter," said one of the guards.

30
00:02:01.838 --> 00:02:06.814
The Tang Monk and his companions reached a large hall.

31
00:02:06.815 --> 00:02:10.782
Buddha sat at the opposite end of the hall.

32
00:02:10.783 --> 00:02:15.052
Other buddhas and bodhisattvas stood behind him.

33
00:02:15.053 --> 00:02:19.876
Guanyin was standing next to Buddha and smiling.

34
00:02:19.877 --> 00:02:22.481
The travelers bowed.

35
00:02:22.482 --> 00:02:25.789
"Congratulations," said Buddha.

36
00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:30.802
[g@"You have all traveled far and faced many challenges.

37
00:02:30.803 --> 00:02:34.231
You have done well."@g]

38
00:02:34.232 --> 00:02:36.628
[g@Wukong's heart swelled.

39
00:02:36.629 --> 00:02:39.787
He wiped a tear from his eye.@g]

40
00:02:39.788 --> 00:02:41.939
[g@"Thank you," said the Tang Monk.

41
00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.364
"It was an honor to make the journey."@g]

42
00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:50.300
Servants brought a meal to the travelers.

43
00:02:50.301 --> 00:02:58.043
When the travelers were done eating, a guard led them to a large room filled with magical light and mist.

44
00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:03.574
[g@Wooden chests lined the walls.

45
00:03:03.575 --> 00:03:09.311
Inside the chests were countless scrolls.@g]

46
00:03:09.312 --> 00:03:13.036
"Marvelous," the Tang Monk murmured.

47
00:03:13.037 --> 00:03:18.510
"The True Scriptures are written on these scrolls," said the guard.

48
00:03:18.511 --> 00:03:23.676
He picked out three scrolls and handed them to the Tang Monk.

49
00:03:23.677 --> 00:03:28.893
Speechless, the monk gazed at the scrolls.

50
00:03:28.894 --> 00:03:33.885
Then he handed them to Wujing and Bajie.

51
00:03:33.886 --> 00:03:44.062
The two spirits carefully wrapped the scrolls and placed them in a bag.

52
00:03:44.063 --> 00:03:47.989
Again the travelers bowed before Buddha.

53
00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:53.400
"Take the True Scriptures back to the Tang Empire," said Buddha.

54
00:03:53.401 --> 00:03:57.939
"Ugh, another long journey," Bajie murmured.

55
00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:02.255
"Stop complaining, Bajie," whispered Wukong.

56
00:04:02.256 --> 00:04:04.011
[g@Bajie whispered back.

57
00:04:04.012 --> 00:04:07.826
"Don't tell me what to do."@g]

58
00:04:07.827 --> 00:04:12.321
"Both of you, stop arguing!" whispered Wujing.

59
00:04:12.322 --> 00:04:14.496
Buddha was still talking.

60
00:04:14.497 --> 00:04:20.798
"The scriptures will teach the people there to be good and to treat each other kindly.

61
00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:23.223
[g@But take good care of the scriptures.

62
00:04:23.224 --> 00:04:25.995
They are extremely valuable.@g]

63
00:04:25.996 --> 00:04:32.662
Once you have delivered them, you shall come back here to receive your rewards."

64
00:04:32.663 --> 00:04:36.183
"Don't worry, Buddha," said Wukong.

65
00:04:36.184 --> 00:04:39.893
"We will protect the scriptures with our lives."

66
00:04:39.894 --> 00:04:44.752
A guard offered to carry the travelers to the Tang Empire.

67
00:04:44.753 --> 00:04:47.146
"Thank you," said the Tang Monk.

68
00:04:47.147 --> 00:04:56.538
"What a relief!" said Bajie.

69
00:04:56.539 --> 00:05:02.827
The guard recited a spell and then flew out of the monastery with the travelers.

70
00:05:02.828 --> 00:05:05.053
[g@Buddha turned to Guanyin.

71
00:05:05.054 --> 00:05:09.210
"The Tang Monk and his companions have done well."@g]

72
00:05:09.211 --> 00:05:10.790
[g@Guanyin nodded.

73
00:05:10.791 --> 00:05:14.587
"Wukong especially has learned a lot during the journey.@g]

74
00:05:14.588 --> 00:05:16.888
[g@He isn't violent anymore.

75
00:05:16.889 --> 00:05:20.903
I believe he is now a good Buddhist."@g]

76
00:05:20.904 --> 00:05:24.922
Just then a messenger ran into the hall.

77
00:05:24.923 --> 00:05:34.399
"Bodhisattva!" he cried. "We have a problem!"

